      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The inconsistency arises because different types of language trigger different policy concerns. While Post 2 uses coded language common in nationalist discourse, the presence of strong, direct generalizations in Post 4 (which I implicitly grouped with 1) often triggers immediate toxicity flags. Post 2's vague framing allows it to exist in a borderline category that requires deeper contextual review, while slang in Post 1 often violates policies against targeted antagonism. Your metric needs to clarify if coded political rhetoric is weighted equally to direct insults.",
